🔹 2. Framework
-A framework is a set of classes and interfaces which provide
ready-made architecture
-It provides a pre-defined way to build programs.
You don’t need to write everything from scratch.
Examples:
Spring (for web apps)
Java Swing (for GUI apps)
Think of it as a toolkit with instructions.
____________________________________________
🔹 3. Collection Framework
-is an API(classes and interface library)
-A Collection Framework is a set of ready-made classes and interfaces in Java.
-It helps store, manage, and manipulate groups of objects easily.
-Instead of writing your own logic to handle objects,
you can use this framework..
-store multiple object together
-Provides ready-made methods to:
Add objects
Remove objects
Search objects
Sort objects
-Part of the java.util package.
Examples:
ArrayList (list of things)
HashSet (unique items)
HashMap (key-value pairs)
- container for objects.